<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net">
  <diagram name="System Design" id="system-design">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2600" pageHeight="6000" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>

        <mxCell id="2" value="LLM Serving Platform (ChatGPT-style Inference Service)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=22;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="20" width="1200" height="44" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="3" value="Difficulty: 5/5 (Hard)  ·  2026-08-22" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=13;fontColor=#666666;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="66" width="700" height="26" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============================== CANDIDATE SECTION ============================== -->
        <mxCell id="10" value="CANDIDATE DESIGN  (exactly as described in the round)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=17;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1F5C99;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="140" width="1000" height="32" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="11" value="" style="line;strokeWidth=2;html=1;strokeColor=#1F5C99;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="176" width="2480" height="10" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="12" value="Functional Requirements" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="216" width="400" height="28" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="13" value="1. A user sends a conversation (chat history + new message). The service runs it through a large language&#10;    model and streams the generated tokens back to the user's browser as they are produced.&#10;&#10;2. Output tokens should be streamed to the user as they are generated.&#10;&#10;3. A ChatCompletion request is handled by models running on GPUs, which are expensive, scarce and slow to&#10;    provision. The system must provision GPUs if needed and load model weights into GPUs for inference.&#10;&#10;4. Multiple model sizes offered; multiple tiers of service — paying tier gets better service than free tier." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;fillColor=#EAF2FA;strokeColor=#1F5C99;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="252" width="1180" height="230" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="14" value="Non-Functional Requirements" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1320" y="216" width="400" height="28" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="15" value="(not produced — the round ended before NFRs)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=14;fillColor=#F5F5F5;strokeColor=#B3B3B3;fontColor=#777777;dashed=1;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1320" y="252" width="620" height="70" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="16" value="Core Entities  ·  API Design  ·  High-Level Design  ·  Deep Dive&#10;&#10;(not reached — the round was abandoned inside the requirements phase)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=14;fillColor=#F5F5F5;strokeColor=#B3B3B3;fontColor=#777777;dashed=1;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1320" y="362" width="620" height="120" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============================== OPTIMAL SECTION ============================== -->
        <mxCell id="100" value="OPTIMAL REFERENCE  (what a senior strong-hire would design)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=17;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1A7F37;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="640" width="1100" height="32" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="101" value="" style="line;strokeWidth=2;html=1;strokeColor=#1A7F37;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="676" width="2480" height="10" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!--  Band 1: Requirements -->
        <mxCell id="110" value="1 · Requirements" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="730" width="400" height="28" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="111" value="&lt;b&gt;FRs — choices, not restatements&lt;/b&gt;&#10;&#10;• Submit a conversation → receive a streamed completion&#10;&#10;• Cancel an in-flight generation&#10;   (users hit stop constantly = live GPU spend)&#10;&#10;• Reconnect / resume a stream that dropped mid-generation&#10;&#10;• Route to a requested model (small / large)&#10;&#10;• Per-tier admission, priority and shedding under scarcity&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Out of scope — say it aloud&lt;/b&gt;&#10;&#10;training &amp;amp; fine-tuning · conversation persistence&#10;the model itself · safety filtering · billing &amp;amp; metering · auth" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;fillColor=#E8F5EC;strokeColor=#1A7F37;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="770" width="800" height="420" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="112" value="&lt;b&gt;NFRs — three distinct latencies, and they trade against each other&lt;/b&gt;&#10;&#10;• &lt;b&gt;TTFT&lt;/b&gt; (time to first token): p99 &amp;lt; 1s paid, &amp;lt; 5s free — perceived responsiveness&#10;• &lt;b&gt;TPOT&lt;/b&gt; (inter-token): ~50 ms/token — must beat reading speed or the stream stutters&#10;• &lt;b&gt;Total generation&lt;/b&gt;: 500 tokens x 50 ms = 25 s of &lt;i&gt;held GPU&lt;/i&gt; per request&#10;• Availability 99.9% on submit; a dropped stream is resumable, not a data-loss event&#10;• Consistency: not a factor — no shared mutable state on the serving path&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Scale (givens)&lt;/b&gt;&#10;100M DAU · 10 msgs/user/day · 1,000 in / 500 out tokens per message&#10;peak 3x average · 90% of traffic to the small model&#10;a large-model GPU generates ~2,000 output tok/s aggregate across concurrent requests&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;THE TRAP:  QPS is the wrong unit.&lt;/b&gt;&#10;Capacity is tokens/second, and requests differ ~100x in cost.&#10;Sizing this fleet in requests/sec produces a fleet wrong by an order of magnitude.&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Derivation&lt;/b&gt;  (day = 10^5 s)&#10;&#10;1e9 msgs/day  →  1e4 msgs/s average  →  3e4 msgs/s at peak&#10;output tokens at peak:  3e4/s x 500  =  1.5e7 output tok/s&#10;GPUs  ≈  1.5e7 / 2e3  ≈  &lt;b&gt;7,500 GPUs&lt;/b&gt; at peak for generation alone (prefill on top)&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Conclusion:&lt;/b&gt; cost dominates every other concern → batching, tiering and KV-cache reuse&#10;are &lt;i&gt;necessary&lt;/i&gt;, not decorative. If the 2,000 tok/s figure is off by 10x, the fleet moves 10x&#10;and the entire business case moves with it." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;fillColor=#E8F5EC;strokeColor=#1A7F37;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="900" y="770" width="1160" height="620" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!--  Band 2: Core entities -->
        <mxCell id="120" value="2 · Core Entities" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1500" width="400" height="28" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="121" value="&lt;b&gt;Request&lt;/b&gt;&#10;&#10;requestId  (idempotency key)&#10;userId, tier&#10;modelId&#10;messages[]  (role, content)&#10;maxTokens, temperature&#10;promptTokenCount (est.)&#10;state:&#10;   QUEUED | PREFILL | DECODING&#10;   | DONE | CANCELLED | FAILED&#10;assignedWorkerId&#10;createdAt, firstTokenAt" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;fillColor=#E8F5EC;strokeColor=#1A7F37;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1540" width="440" height="300" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="122" value="&lt;b&gt;Model&lt;/b&gt;&#10;&#10;modelId, version&#10;weightsUri  (object store)&#10;paramCount, dtype&#10;gpuMemForWeights&#10;&lt;b&gt;kvBytesPerToken&lt;/b&gt;&#10;   ← the field that decides&#10;      admission control&#10;maxContextLen&#10;warmPoolTarget" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;fillColor=#E8F5EC;strokeColor=#1A7F37;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="540" y="1540" width="440" height="300" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="123" value="&lt;b&gt;InferenceWorker&lt;/b&gt;   (NOT stateless)&#10;&#10;workerId, gpuType, zone&#10;loadedModelId  (or null)&#10;state:&#10;   PROVISIONING | LOADING&#10;   | READY | DRAINING | DEAD&#10;totalKvBytes / freeKvBytes&#10;activeRequestIds[]&#10;currentBatchSize&#10;observedTokensPerSec&#10;heartbeatAt" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;fillColor=#E8F5EC;strokeColor=#1A7F37;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1040" y="1540" width="460" height="300" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="124" value="&lt;b&gt;StreamSession&lt;/b&gt;&#10;&#10;requestId&#10;tokensEmitted  (monotonic seq)&#10;lastAckedSeq&#10;   ← enables resume-from-offset&#10;bufferedTail  (ring buffer)&#10;connectionState&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;QueueEntry&lt;/b&gt;&#10;&#10;requestId, priorityClass&#10;enqueuedAt, deadline" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;fillColor=#E8F5EC;strokeColor=#1A7F37;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1560" y="1540" width="440" height="300" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!--  Band 3: API -->
        <mxCell id="130" value="3 · API Design" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1950" width="400" height="28" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="131" value="&lt;b&gt;POST /v1/chat/completions&lt;/b&gt;      (SSE stream · Authorization: Bearer &amp;lt;jwt&amp;gt;  →  userId + tier)&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Headers:&lt;/b&gt;   Idempotency-Key: &amp;lt;uuid&amp;gt;      ← a retry of a 25-second request must NOT double-charge a GPU&#10;&lt;b&gt;Request:&lt;/b&gt;   { model, messages: [{ role, content }], maxTokens, temperature, stream: true }&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Response 200 · text/event-stream:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;      event: meta     data: { requestId, model, queuePositionHint }&#10;                                              ← requestId is load-bearing: it is the cancel + resume key&#10;      event: token    data: { seq, text }     ← seq is load-bearing: it is the resume offset&#10;      event: done     data: { finishReason: stop | length | cancelled | error,&#10;                                          usage: { promptTokens, completionTokens } }&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Errors:&lt;/b&gt;   400 bad request · 401 unauthenticated · 413 context too long · 429 tier rate limit (Retry-After)&#10;               503 capacity exhausted — free tier sheds here first, paid tier queues instead&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;GET /v1/chat/completions/{requestId}/stream?fromSeq=N&lt;/b&gt;     → resume a dropped stream from seq N (same event shape)&#10;&lt;b&gt;DELETE /v1/chat/completions/{requestId}&lt;/b&gt;                              → cancel in flight; 202, frees the KV cache immediately&#10;&lt;b&gt;GET /v1/models&lt;/b&gt;                                                                    → [{ modelId, maxContextLen, availableToTier }]&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Why SSE over WebSocket&lt;/b&gt; — the stream is unidirectional server→client, so SSE gets HTTP/2 multiplexing, proxy&#10;compatibility and automatic browser reconnect (Last-Event-ID maps straight onto fromSeq). &lt;b&gt;Given up:&lt;/b&gt; no client→server&#10;channel, so cancel needs a separate DELETE rather than an in-band frame.&#10;&lt;b&gt;Why not long-polling&lt;/b&gt; — a token every 50 ms would mean 20 round-trips per second per user." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;fillColor=#E8F5EC;strokeColor=#1A7F37;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1990" width="1960" height="560" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!--  Band 4: HLD -->
        <mxCell id="140" value="4 · High-Level Design" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="2660" width="400" height="28" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="139" value="request path  ──▶            token path  ┈┈▶" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=12;fontColor=#666666;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="480" y="2660" width="600" height="28" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="141" value="Browser" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="2910" width="180" height="90" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="142" value="API Gateway&#10;&#10;auth · tier lookup&#10;per-tier rate limit" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="340" y="2885" width="220" height="140" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="143" value="Stream Gateway&#10;&#10;stateless SSE front&#10;holds the client conn&#10;relays tokens&#10;resume-from-seq buffer" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF4E5;strokeColor=#B36B00;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="660" y="2870" width="260" height="170" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="144" value="Priority Queue&#10;(Redis / Kafka)&#10;&#10;paid · free · batch&#10;deadline-aware" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF4E5;strokeColor=#B36B00;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1020" y="2880" width="240" height="150" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="145" value="Scheduler / Router&#10;&#10;• picks a worker with the right model&#10;   LOADED and enough FREE KV memory&#10;• admission = memory admission&#10;• prefix-affinity routing (cache hit)&#10;• emits shed / 503 when starved" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFE5E5;strokeColor=#C0392B;align=left;spacingLeft=12;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=12;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1360" y="2845" width="400" height="220" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="146" value="Inference Worker Fleet (GPU) — STATEFUL&#10;&#10;• continuous batching: every step decodes&#10;   one token for every request in the batch&#10;• KV cache per request stays resident in GPU&#10;   RAM for the whole generation (GBs)&#10;   → you cannot round-robin&#10;• paged KV blocks (vLLM-style) to stop&#10;   fragmentation stranding capacity&#10;• streams tokens back over gRPC" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFE5E5;strokeColor=#C0392B;align=left;spacingLeft=12;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=12;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1860" y="2825" width="440" height="260" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="150" value="Worker Registry&#10;(etcd / Redis)&#10;&#10;heartbeat · loadedModel&#10;freeKvBytes" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E5EEFF;strokeColor=#1F5C99;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="3300" width="360" height="160" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="149" value="Model Registry&#10;+ Weights in Object Storage&#10;&#10;S3 / Blob → pulled to local NVMe,&#10;peer-to-peer seeded on scale-out" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E5EEFF;strokeColor=#1F5C99;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="540" y="3300" width="400" height="160" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="148" value="Capacity Controller&#10;&#10;• warm pool per model&#10;• scales on queue depth &amp;amp; TTFT,&#10;   NOT on GPU utilisation&#10;• provisions node (minutes) →&#10;   loads weights (1–5 min)&#10;• predictive diurnal pre-warm" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E5EEFF;strokeColor=#1F5C99;align=left;spacingLeft=12;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=12;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1060" y="3270" width="380" height="220" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="147" value="Prefix / KV Cache Store&#10;&#10;shared system-prompt and&#10;conversation-prefix reuse&#10;→ cuts prefill cost and TTFT" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E5EEFF;strokeColor=#1F5C99;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1860" y="3300" width="400" height="160" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="151" value="Metrics &amp;amp; Usage Sink&#10;&#10;TTFT / TPOT per tier · queue depth&#10;tokens billed · GPU $ per M tokens" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F0E5FF;strokeColor=#6B3FA0;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="3660" width="400" height="150" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- HLD edges: request path -->
        <mxCell id="160" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeWidth=1.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="141" target="142">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="161" value="POST /chat/completions" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;fontSize=11;strokeWidth=1.5;verticalAlign=bottom;" edge="1" parent="1" source="142" target="143">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="162" value="enqueue (priority = tier)" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;fontSize=11;strokeWidth=1.5;verticalAlign=bottom;" edge="1" parent="1" source="143" target="144">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="163" value="dequeue" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;fontSize=11;strokeWidth=1.5;verticalAlign=bottom;" edge="1" parent="1" source="144" target="145">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="164" value="dispatch if KV fits" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;fontSize=11;strokeWidth=1.5;verticalAlign=bottom;" edge="1" parent="1" source="145" target="146">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- HLD edges: token return path (own lane above the row) -->
        <mxCell id="165" value="token stream (gRPC, seq-numbered)" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.75;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;fontSize=11;dashed=1;strokeColor=#C0392B;strokeWidth=1.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="146" target="143">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points"><mxPoint x="2080" y="2740"/><mxPoint x="855" y="2740"/></Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="166" value="SSE tokens" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=0.25;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;fontSize=11;dashed=1;strokeColor=#C0392B;strokeWidth=1.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="143" target="141">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points"><mxPoint x="725" y="2800"/><mxPoint x="150" y="2800"/></Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- HLD edges: control plane -->
        <mxCell id="167" value="prefix lookup / insert" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;fontSize=11;strokeWidth=1.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="146" target="147">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="168" value="queue depth + TTFT" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=0.25;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;fontSize=11;strokeWidth=1.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="145" target="148">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="169" value="provision node + load weights" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.25;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.75;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;fontSize=11;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="148" target="146">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1610" y="3325"/><mxPoint x="1610" y="3170"/><mxPoint x="1800" y="3170"/><mxPoint x="1800" y="3020"/></Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="170" value="pull weights" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;fontSize=11;strokeWidth=1.5;verticalAlign=bottom;" edge="1" parent="1" source="149" target="148">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="171" value="heartbeat / freeKvBytes" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;fontSize=11;strokeWidth=1.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="146" target="150">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points"><mxPoint x="2080" y="3560"/><mxPoint x="480" y="3560"/><mxPoint x="480" y="3380"/></Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="172" value="worker state" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.75;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;fontSize=11;strokeWidth=1.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="150" target="145">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points"><mxPoint x="240" y="3180"/><mxPoint x="1300" y="3180"/><mxPoint x="1300" y="3010"/></Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="173" value="latency + usage events" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;fontSize=11;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="150" target="151">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!--  Band 5: Trade-offs -->
        <mxCell id="180" value="5 · Key Trade-offs  (each against a NAMED alternative)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="3960" width="800" height="28" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="181" value="&lt;b&gt;Continuous batching&lt;/b&gt;   vs static batching   vs no batching&#10;&#10;Static batching wastes the GPU: the whole batch waits for the longest generation in it. No batching wastes it far worse — a single&#10;decode step underutilises the device by roughly 50x. Continuous batching admits and evicts requests per token step.&#10;&lt;b&gt;Given up:&lt;/b&gt; the scheduler is now on the critical path of every token, and per-request latency depends on who else is in the batch&#10;— a noisy-neighbour effect you must bound with a maximum batch size." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;fillColor=#E8F5EC;strokeColor=#1A7F37;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="4000" width="1960" height="170" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="182" value="&lt;b&gt;Stateful workers + affinity routing&lt;/b&gt;   vs stateless round-robin&#10;&#10;Round-robin is impossible mid-generation: the KV cache lives on one specific GPU. Affinity also buys prefix-cache hits.&#10;&lt;b&gt;Given up:&lt;/b&gt; load balancing gets genuinely hard, a node loss kills every in-flight stream on it, and draining a worker takes&#10;up to a full generation (~25 s) to complete." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;fillColor=#E8F5EC;strokeColor=#1A7F37;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="4210" width="1960" height="150" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="183" value="&lt;b&gt;Warm pool&lt;/b&gt;   vs pure on-demand scale-out&#10;&#10;Provisioning (minutes) plus weight loading (1–5 min) is far longer than any acceptable TTFT, so autoscaling cannot &lt;i&gt;react&lt;/i&gt; to a&#10;spike — it has to anticipate it. &lt;b&gt;Given up:&lt;/b&gt; you pay for idle GPUs. Quantify it: at ~7,500 peak GPUs a 15% warm buffer is&#10;~1,100 idle GPUs — a real line item, and one you justify explicitly against the alternative of shedding that traffic." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;fillColor=#E8F5EC;strokeColor=#1A7F37;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="4400" width="1960" height="150" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="184" value="&lt;b&gt;Strict priority queue with shedding&lt;/b&gt;   vs fair-share   vs first-come-first-served&#10;&#10;FCFS lets free traffic starve the paid SLO. Fair-share protects nobody's p99. Strict priority plus free-tier shedding is what&#10;actually meets the paid TTFT target. &lt;b&gt;Given up:&lt;/b&gt; free-tier starvation under sustained load — bound it with a reserved floor of&#10;capacity so free never drops to literally zero.&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;SSE&lt;/b&gt; vs WebSocket vs long-polling — argued in the API section: HTTP/2 multiplexing and native browser reconnect, at the cost&#10;of no client→server channel." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;fillColor=#E8F5EC;strokeColor=#1A7F37;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="4590" width="1960" height="200" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!--  Band 6: Deep dives -->
        <mxCell id="190" value="6 · Deep Dives" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="4900" width="400" height="28" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="191" value="&lt;b&gt;A. The core hard problem — GPU memory is the real scheduler&lt;/b&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Naive:&lt;/b&gt; route to the least-loaded worker by request count.&#10;&lt;b&gt;Break:&lt;/b&gt; requests are not equal. A 100k-context request's KV cache can be 100x&#10;a short one's. Counting requests overcommits GPU RAM → OOM mid-generation&#10;→ every stream on that worker dies at once.&#10;&lt;b&gt;Fix:&lt;/b&gt; admit on &lt;i&gt;bytes&lt;/i&gt;: kvBytesPerToken x (promptLen + maxTokens) must fit in&#10;freeKvBytes before dispatch. Paged KV blocks so memory is allocated incrementally&#10;and fragmentation cannot strand capacity. Preemption policy: evict and requeue&#10;the newest low-priority request rather than OOM the box.&#10;&lt;b&gt;Trade-off:&lt;/b&gt; reserving for maxTokens over-reserves for requests that stop early;&#10;incremental paging recovers that but risks a mid-flight allocation failure." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;fillColor=#E8F5EC;strokeColor=#1A7F37;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="4940" width="960" height="330" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="192" value="&lt;b&gt;B. The scale break — 10x traffic, or one viral moment&lt;/b&gt;&#10;&#10;At 3e4 msg/s peak the fleet is ~7,500 GPUs. Push 10x and there is simply no fleet&#10;to buy: GPU supply is a &lt;b&gt;hard external ceiling&lt;/b&gt;, unlike every other system where&#10;you just add nodes. So the design must degrade rather than scale:&#10;&#10;   • shed free tier first (503 + Retry-After)&#10;   • then downgrade remaining free traffic to the small model&#10;   • then cap maxTokens per request&#10;   • queue paid traffic against a deadline; surface an honest queue position&#10;   • multi-region overflow routing to wherever capacity actually exists&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;This is the senior conversation: the fix is admission policy, not capacity.&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;fillColor=#E8F5EC;strokeColor=#1A7F37;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1060" y="4940" width="940" height="330" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="193" value="&lt;b&gt;C. Hot keys / hot partitions&lt;/b&gt;&#10;&#10;• &lt;b&gt;Long-context requests are the hot key&lt;/b&gt; — they monopolise KV memory. Isolate&#10;   them onto a dedicated long-context pool so they cannot starve short chats.&#10;&#10;• A single shared system prompt is a hot &lt;i&gt;prefix&lt;/i&gt; — that is a gift, not a problem:&#10;   cache its KV once per worker and skip prefill for it entirely.&#10;&#10;• Model skew: 90% small / 10% large means the fleet split must be dynamic, or the&#10;   large-model pool sits idle while small-model requests queue." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;fillColor=#E8F5EC;strokeColor=#1A7F37;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="5330" width="960" height="270" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="194" value="&lt;b&gt;D. Failure of an in-flight stream&lt;/b&gt;&#10;&#10;A worker dies at token 300 of 500. The KV cache is gone and cannot be recovered.&#10;Options: (i) restart the generation from scratch on another worker — correct, but the&#10;user sees a stutter and you pay for the tokens twice; (ii) fail the request outright.&#10;Choose (i) for paid, (ii) for free. The client resumes via fromSeq and the gateway&#10;replays its buffered tail, so the user sees a pause rather than a broken answer.&#10;Non-determinism means a restart may produce different text — pin the sampling seed&#10;per requestId so the replayed continuation is coherent with what was already shown." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;fillColor=#E8F5EC;strokeColor=#1A7F37;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1060" y="5330" width="940" height="270" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="195" value="&lt;b&gt;E. Operability — how do you know it is wrong?&lt;/b&gt;&#10;&#10;• Alert on &lt;b&gt;queue depth and TTFT p99 per tier&lt;/b&gt;, never on GPU utilisation — a healthy batched GPU is pinned at 100% by design,&#10;   so utilisation carries no signal at all.&#10;• Track &lt;b&gt;TPOT p99&lt;/b&gt;: a rising inter-token latency means batches have grown too large.&#10;• Track &lt;b&gt;KV-memory headroom&lt;/b&gt; per worker and the preemption rate.&#10;• Track &lt;b&gt;$ per million tokens&lt;/b&gt; as a first-class SLO — at this fleet size cost IS a health metric.&#10;• Watch weight-load time and warm-pool hit rate: a cold-start storm is invisible in request metrics until TTFT has already blown&#10;   through the SLO." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;fillColor=#E8F5EC;strokeColor=#1A7F37;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="5660" width="1960" height="220" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
